"{{Term/Store|Zora Stone Monuments||Series, BotW}}" is a [[Side Quest]] in {{BotW}}.<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Zora Stone Monuments}}<br/>{{Color BotW|Side Quest|Zora's Domain}}|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref>

==Overview==
After calming [[Divine Beast Vah Ruta]], [[Link]] will be able to speak with [[Jiahto]] in the [[Sleeping Chamber]] of [[Zora's Domain]]. He apologizes for not introducing himself sooner, explaining that he is a historian who studies and preserves [[Zora]] history.<ref>{{Cite|Oh! I am sorry I did not introduce myself sooner. I am Jiahto. I am a historian who studies Zora history and preserves it for future generations.|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref> However, the [[Stone Monument]] found in the Sleeping Chamber is in a deteriorated state, and he fears the rest are just as bad.<ref>{{Cite|Even so, this stone monument that King Dorephan supposedly wrote... It's torn to pieces now. Most likely, the {{Color BotW|Red|10 stone monuments}} outside of the domain are in the same awful condition.|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref>

Jiahto wants to compile the contents of the Stone Monuments into a [[Book]], but due to his old age, traveling to all 10 of them would be difficult.<ref>{{Cite|I'm thinking of collecting the contents of all of the stone monuments and compiling them into a book. But with these old legs and fins, traveling to all {{Color BotW|Red|10 stone monuments}} will take a great deal of time.|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref> Therefore, he asks Link to find all of the Stone Monuments and report their contents to him.<ref>{{Cite|That is why... Link... I'd like to ask a favor of you. I'd like you to find all {{Color BotW|Red|10 stone monuments}} around {{Color BotW|Blue|Zora's Domain}} and tell me what they say.|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref> If Link accepts this task, Jiahto will be grateful.<ref>{{Cite|Oh! Thank you! You truly are a lifesaver! How reassuring that the Champion will search for those monuments for me!|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref> He also shares a rumor that one of the Stone Monuments has the location of a treasure written on it, and should Link find it, he would be allowed to keep it.<ref>{{Cite|I have it on good authority that among the stone monuments, one has the location of some {{Color BotW|Red|treasure}} written on it. If you happen to find said {{Color BotW|Red|treasure}}, feel free to keep it. It will most likely be something that a Zora wouldn't need.|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref> He reminds Link that the 10 Monuments are located around Zora's Domain,<ref>{{Cite|Yes, you'll find the {{Color BotW|Red|10 stone monuments}} around {{Color BotW|Blue|Zora's Domain}}... I believe in you. In fact, I'm counting on you!|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref> and the [[Side Quest]] will begin.

The Stone Monuments can be found at the following locations:

{{Data Table Copy
|fromPage= Stone Monument
|storedAs= Monuments
}}

After locating and reading all 10 Stone Monuments, Link can return to Zora's Domain to share their contents with Jiahto.<ref>{{Cite|Link... It would seem you have checked all of the stone monuments for me! Now then, please tell me what was written on them!|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref> He is amazed by the tales inscribed on the Stone Monuments that Link has helped gather for him.<ref>{{Cite|Hmm... The history, culture, folklore, and various heroic acts of the proud Zora people... It's all here! Eureka! Thanks to you, I've compiled the precious information from those stone monuments!|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref> As a reward, Jiahto gives Link a [[Diamond]].<ref>{{Cite|Link, thank you for taking on such an arduous task! Please, allow me to reward you!|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref>{{Note|If Link does not have the [[Inventory]] space for another Diamond, Jiahto will hold onto his reward until he can take it.<ref>{{Cite|I would like to reward you, but it seems you already have quite a collection of {{Color BotW|Blue|diamonds}}. Since you cannot carry any more, I suggest you somehow rid yourself of one and come back.|Jiahto|BotW}}</ref>}} Once this is done, "Zora Stone Monuments" will be completed.

